# REGRESSION — a mutation spelled inside an `assert` must reach the CoW prescan.
#
# `cow_after_stmt` (src/ir/lowering/functions.rs) handled 16 of 29 `Stmt` forms
# and swept 13 into `_ => {}`, so a mutation inside one of them was never
# recorded and a live view into the mutated collection was not rescued.
# Measured at pristine HEAD: rc 139 on BOTH backends, against an rc-0 control
# differing only in the statement form wrapping the same call.
#
# ⚠ THE LINT WAS GREEN THE WHOLE TIME. `cow_after_stmt_covers_block_bearing_variants`
# takes BLOCK-bearing variants as its subject; `Assert` is EXPRESSION-bearing,
# so no widening of its list could ever have caught this — the subject was the
# wrong set (AGENTS.md Core #15e Q4). What retires the class is the match being
# EXHAUSTIVE: a new `Stmt` variant is now a compile error in that function.
#
# ⚠ The realloc is load-bearing: 64 pushes with a heap-forced payload from
# `mk`. Fewer pushes or a literal is rc 0 even with the bug present.
String mk(String a, String b):
    return a + b

int grow(Vector[String] &vv):
    vv.push(mk("fillfillfillfill", "ererererererer"))
    return 1

void main():
    Vector[String] v = []
    v.push(mk("hel", "lo"))
    String s = v.get(0).unwrap()
    int i = 0
    while i < 64:
        assert grow(&v) == 1
        i = i + 1
    print(s)
